<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 1996 investments down by 4.4 pct from 1995.</title>
<headline>Hungary 1996 investments down by 4.4 pct from 1995.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment in Hungary totalled 1,199.7 forints in 1996, down by 4.4 percent in real terms from 1995, the Central Statistical Office (KSH) said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY INVESTMENTS IN BRANCHES OF THE ECONOMY (HUF bln)</p>
<p>						   1996	   1995</p>
<p> Agriculture, forestry, fishing	  36.8	   31.3</p>
<p> Mining					   4.0	    4.1</p>
<p> Processing industry			287.6	  218.7</p>
<p>Electricity-, gas-, water-</p>
<p>  distribution, district heating	 89.2	   89.5</p>
<p> Construction industry		     41.1	   24.5</p>
<p> Trade, maintenance services	     69.9	   44.3</p>
<p> Hotel and catering			   8.4	    8.7</p>
<p>Transport, post, telecommunications,</p>
<p>  warehousing				 196.4	  189.9</p>
<p> Financial services			  33.1	   41.0</p>
<p>Real estate, leasing,</p>
<p>  business support services	     310.4	  227.4</p>
<p>Public administration,</p>
<p>  social security			    33.8	   32.1</p>
<p> Education				     22.5	   25.8</p>
<p> Health and social care		    26.2	   31.0</p>
<p>Other social, communal</p>
<p>  or personal services		     40.2	   34.5 @</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> TOTAL					1,199.7	1,003.0</p>
<p>MATERIAL COMPOSITION OF HUNGARY INVESTMENTS</p>
<p>			1996 (HUF bln)	1996 pct change from 1995</p>
<p> Buildings	    643.6			    -1.0</p>
<p> Machinery	    455.4			    -7.8</p>
<p>  -Imported	   197.9			    +1.2</p>
<p>  -Domestic	   257.6			   -14.8</p>
<p> Other		  100.6			    -9.9</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> TOTAL		1,199.7			    -4.4 @</p>
<p>NOTE: The KSH said that the volume of investments in the fourth quarter of 1996 rose six percent year-on-year in real terms, indicating an improving investment climate.</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
